1
00:00:00,554 --> 00:00:00,550
One.

2
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,550
That's how many Hyundai Ioniq 9s were
sold in the whole of Australia in

3
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:06,370
September 2026.

4
00:00:06,420 --> 00:00:09,350
One car, in a country of
twenty-seven million people.

5
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:14,017
A big, seven-seat electric family SUV
that costs well over a hundred thousand

6
00:00:14,067 --> 00:00:17,910
dollars drive-away in top spec,
and one buyer in an entire month.

7
00:00:17,960 --> 00:00:19,130
And it's not alone.

8
00:00:19,180 --> 00:00:22,970
That month, seventy-nine different
makes and models recorded zero sales.

9
00:00:23,020 --> 00:00:23,770
Not one.

10
00:00:23,820 --> 00:00:26,390
Plenty more limped along
with two, three or five.

11
00:00:26,440 --> 00:00:29,030
And while the market as
a whole actually grew,

12
00:00:29,080 --> 00:00:32,250
some of the biggest names in the business
are watching certain models fall off

13
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:35,310
a cliff and they're slashing
prices to try to move them.

14
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:36,290
So in this video,

15
00:00:36,340 --> 00:00:39,870
I'm counting down twelve new cars that
Australians simply aren't buying right

16
00:00:39,920 --> 00:00:40,570
now.

17
00:00:40,620 --> 00:00:43,450
These are real sales numbers
from the official industry data,

18
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:46,670
and I'll show you the price cuts
and the excuses behind them.

19
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:50,430
I'll also show you a few cars that look
like disasters on paper but actually

20
00:00:50,480 --> 00:00:52,850
aren't because that
matters if you're shopping.

21
00:00:52,900 --> 00:00:53,850
And at the end,

22
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:57,050
I'll tell you how to use all of this
to get a better deal or how to avoid

23
00:00:57,100 --> 00:00:57,960
getting burned.

24
00:00:58,586 --> 00:01:02,436
First, the big picture, because it
explains everything that follows.

25
00:01:02,486 --> 00:01:08,536
Australians bought 108,778 new
vehicles in September 2026,

26
00:01:08,586 --> 00:01:10,776
according to the official VFACTS figures.

27
00:01:10,826 --> 00:01:14,176
That's up 1.8 per cent on the
same month a year earlier.

28
00:01:14,226 --> 00:01:17,016
So this isn't a market
where nobody is buying cars.

29
00:01:17,066 --> 00:01:19,816
It's a market where
buyers are moving fast.

30
00:01:19,866 --> 00:01:22,336
Electric cars outsold
petrol cars for the month,

31
00:01:22,386 --> 00:01:27,506
with 26,287 sales, up 117 per cent.

32
00:01:27,556 --> 00:01:30,176
Plug-in hybrid sales more than doubled.

33
00:01:30,226 --> 00:01:32,676
Geely's sales jumped 870 per cent.

34
00:01:32,726 --> 00:01:36,016
BYD finished second
overall, behind only Toyota.

35
00:01:36,066 --> 00:01:37,816
And look at which models are winning.

36
00:01:37,866 --> 00:01:41,976
The Ford Ranger was the
country's best seller with 5,062.

37
00:01:42,026 --> 00:01:46,316
Then the Toyota RAV4, the Tesla
Model Y and the Toyota HiLux.

38
00:01:46,366 --> 00:01:50,376
But right behind them: the
BYD Sealion 7 with 2,687,

39
00:01:50,426 --> 00:01:53,889
the Chery Tiggo 4 with 2,059,

40
00:01:53,939 --> 00:02:00,096
the GWM Haval Jolion with 2,018
and the Geely EX5 with 2,008

41
00:02:00,146 --> 00:02:02,516
up 620 per cent.

42
00:02:02,566 --> 00:02:05,416
Four Chinese models inside
the national top ten.

43
00:02:05,466 --> 00:02:07,196
Now look at who's going backwards.

44
00:02:07,246 --> 00:02:09,776
Subaru, down 42.6 per cent.

45
00:02:09,826 --> 00:02:12,356
Mitsubishi, down 41.5.

46
00:02:12,406 --> 00:02:14,756
Volkswagen, down almost 37.

47
00:02:14,806 --> 00:02:16,276
Nissan, down 30.

48
00:02:16,326 --> 00:02:17,936
Hyundai, down 22.

49
00:02:17,986 --> 00:02:19,996
Kia and Mazda, close to 20 each.

50
00:02:20,046 --> 00:02:23,776
When money moves this quickly,
some cars get left behind.

51
00:02:23,826 --> 00:02:26,356
And a car that stops selling
doesn't just disappear.

52
00:02:26,406 --> 00:02:28,396
It usually sits in a dealer's yard,

53
00:02:28,446 --> 00:02:32,036
often paid for with borrowed money,
losing value every single week.

54
00:02:32,086 --> 00:02:33,656
That's when the discounts start.

55
00:02:33,706 --> 00:02:35,956
A couple of ground rules before the list.

56
00:02:36,006 --> 00:02:39,636
All the monthly figures come from VFACTS
data published through CarExpert's

57
00:02:39,686 --> 00:02:41,396
new-car sales database.

58
00:02:41,446 --> 00:02:43,746
I've only included cars
that are still on sale.

59
00:02:43,796 --> 00:02:45,576
Models that have already been axed,

60
00:02:45,626 --> 00:02:46,856
I'll deal with separately,

61
00:02:46,906 --> 00:02:50,216
because a car that's being run out is
a very different story from a car that

62
00:02:50,266 --> 00:02:51,346
buyers are ignoring.

63
00:02:52,164 --> 00:02:55,394
Number twelve: the Volkswagen ID.4.

64
00:02:55,444 --> 00:02:59,634
Volkswagen's electric SUV found
just 47 buyers in September,

65
00:02:59,684 --> 00:03:02,814
down 73 per cent on the
same month last year.

66
00:03:02,864 --> 00:03:06,834
Its little brother, the T-Cross,
managed 29, down 81 per cent.

67
00:03:06,884 --> 00:03:09,254
And Volkswagen knows it has a problem.

68
00:03:09,304 --> 00:03:10,754
In May 2026,

69
00:03:10,804 --> 00:03:13,284
the director of Volkswagen
Passenger Vehicles Australia,

70
00:03:13,334 --> 00:03:17,254
Piergiorgio Minto, warned about what
happens when sales keep falling.

71
00:03:17,304 --> 00:03:18,374
In his words:

72
00:03:18,424 --> 00:03:22,554
"Whenever you start selling less than
10,000 vehicles a year… you're niche."

73
00:03:22,604 --> 00:03:26,694
Volkswagen sold roughly
29,000 vehicles here in 2025,

74
00:03:26,744 --> 00:03:27,974
down more than 20 per cent.

75
00:03:28,024 --> 00:03:29,594
Keep falling at that rate,

76
00:03:29,644 --> 00:03:32,854
and the brand that gave us the Golf
could become a niche player within five

77
00:03:32,904 --> 00:03:33,734
years.

78
00:03:33,784 --> 00:03:37,574
Volkswagen's product boss, Arjun
Nidigallu, was just as candid.

79
00:03:37,624 --> 00:03:40,714
He admitted that "having that something
for everything hasn't been the case

80
00:03:40,764 --> 00:03:44,134
for a while." The ID.4 is a good example.

81
00:03:44,184 --> 00:03:48,054
It reached Australian showrooms almost
four years after its global debut.

82
00:03:48,104 --> 00:03:52,094
By then, cheaper electric SUVs
from China had already arrived,

83
00:03:52,144 --> 00:03:55,514
with more range, more
screens and lower prices.

84
00:03:55,564 --> 00:03:58,894
Volkswagen has been cutting prices
on its electric range for months,

85
00:03:58,944 --> 00:04:00,074
especially on the ID.

86
00:04:00,124 --> 00:04:00,994
Buzz van.

87
00:04:01,044 --> 00:04:04,894
But when the competition is this
fierce, a discount alone isn't enough.

88
00:04:04,944 --> 00:04:06,994
Number eleven: the Omoda 9.

89
00:04:07,044 --> 00:04:09,874
This is the one that proves
Chinese brands aren't immune.

90
00:04:09,924 --> 00:04:14,754
The Omoda 9 is Omoda Jaecoo's flagship
a big plug-in hybrid SUV with nearly

91
00:04:14,804 --> 00:04:21,514
400 kilowatts, sold in a single trim
at $61,990 before on-road costs.

92
00:04:21,564 --> 00:04:25,574
Last month it found 35
buyers, down 61.5 per cent.

93
00:04:25,624 --> 00:04:27,574
Its own sister models are flying,

94
00:04:27,624 --> 00:04:29,494
but at sixty-two thousand dollars,

95
00:04:29,544 --> 00:04:31,394
buyers are asking a tougher question:

96
00:04:31,444 --> 00:04:35,394
would I rather have a Toyota,
a Kia or a BYD for that money?

97
00:04:35,444 --> 00:04:37,814
Being Chinese is no
longer enough on its own.

98
00:04:37,864 --> 00:04:39,604
The price still has to make sense.

99
00:04:40,493 --> 00:04:43,899
Number ten: the Renault Koleos.

100
00:04:43,949 --> 00:04:46,163
The Koleos is a mid-size family SUV,

101
00:04:46,213 --> 00:04:49,243
the kind of car Australians
buy by the tens of thousands.

102
00:04:49,293 --> 00:04:53,503
Toyota sold more than 4,600
RAV4s in September alone.

103
00:04:53,553 --> 00:04:56,023
Renault found homes for eighteen Koleos.

104
00:04:56,073 --> 00:04:57,983
That's down 70.5 per cent.

105
00:04:58,033 --> 00:05:00,043
And it's not because it's expensive.

106
00:05:00,093 --> 00:05:06,063
The Koleos has been advertised from
$36,990 drive-away cheap for a mid-size

107
00:05:06,113 --> 00:05:08,203
SUV in 2026.

108
00:05:08,253 --> 00:05:11,063
Even at that price, buyers
are walking past it.

109
00:05:11,113 --> 00:05:13,063
This generation has been around for years,

110
00:05:13,113 --> 00:05:17,183
and back in 2025 Renault Australia's
Glen Sealey said a "different vehicle"

111
00:05:17,233 --> 00:05:20,023
may replace it, "maybe in 2026".

112
00:05:20,073 --> 00:05:23,143
Nothing has been confirmed, and
the market has clearly moved on.

113
00:05:23,193 --> 00:05:25,303
That's the first big lesson of this list.

114
00:05:25,353 --> 00:05:28,143
A low price can't save
a car that feels old.

115
00:05:28,193 --> 00:05:32,043
Buyers in 2026 are walking into
showrooms expecting hybrid or electric

116
00:05:32,093 --> 00:05:34,943
options, big screens and
the latest safety tech.

117
00:05:34,993 --> 00:05:37,023
If a car doesn't tick those boxes,

118
00:05:37,073 --> 00:05:38,973
they'll pay a few thousand
more for something newer.

119
00:05:39,023 --> 00:05:41,943
Number nine: the Mazda CX-70.

120
00:05:41,993 --> 00:05:45,463
Mazda's big two-row SUV was
supposed to be a premium flagship.

121
00:05:45,513 --> 00:05:48,983
Instead, it's become one of the
slowest-selling cars in its class.

122
00:05:49,033 --> 00:05:50,823
Sixteen sales in September.

123
00:05:50,873 --> 00:05:53,743
Just 182 for the whole year so far.

124
00:05:53,793 --> 00:05:55,263
To put that in perspective,

125
00:05:55,313 --> 00:05:59,683
Mazda sold more than 3,500 of the
smaller CX-60 over the same period.

126
00:05:59,733 --> 00:06:01,803
In July 2026,

127
00:06:01,853 --> 00:06:07,883
Mazda slashed CX-70 prices
by between $3,700 and $8,051

128
00:06:07,933 --> 00:06:09,203
depending on the variant.

129
00:06:09,253 --> 00:06:10,603
It didn't fix the problem.

130
00:06:10,653 --> 00:06:12,063
And in late October,

131
00:06:12,113 --> 00:06:15,883
Mazda confirmed the CX-70 is ending
production for the United States,

132
00:06:15,933 --> 00:06:17,283
its biggest market.

133
00:06:17,333 --> 00:06:19,723
Mazda Australia says the
car will continue here,

134
00:06:19,773 --> 00:06:22,243
and that it "still has a
small but loyal fanbase".

135
00:06:22,293 --> 00:06:25,803
But unnamed sources told CarsGuide
it will leave the local market soon.

136
00:06:25,853 --> 00:06:29,693
Mazda's own global report has called
Australia a "tough environment".

137
00:06:30,567 --> 00:06:32,517
Number eight: Genesis.

138
00:06:32,567 --> 00:06:35,697
Hyundai's luxury brand has
some genuinely impressive cars,

139
00:06:35,747 --> 00:06:37,337
but the numbers are brutal.

140
00:06:37,387 --> 00:06:42,897
Genesis sold just 66 cars in total
across Australia last month down 54.5 per

141
00:06:42,947 --> 00:06:43,357
cent.

142
00:06:43,407 --> 00:06:45,557
The GV80 wagon moved two.

143
00:06:45,607 --> 00:06:48,837
The GV70, its best seller, managed 46.

144
00:06:48,887 --> 00:06:50,657
The discounts tell the story.

145
00:06:50,707 --> 00:06:55,477
In July, Genesis extended end-of-financial-year
deals with up to $7,000 off

146
00:06:55,527 --> 00:06:59,377
the GV70, and up to $10,000 off the GV80.

147
00:06:59,427 --> 00:07:03,297
That's serious money to take off a
luxury SUV and it still isn't moving them

148
00:07:03,347 --> 00:07:04,717
in big numbers.

149
00:07:04,767 --> 00:07:08,237
Luxury buyers are notoriously
loyal to badges they already know,

150
00:07:08,287 --> 00:07:11,337
like Mercedes-Benz, BMW and Lexus.

151
00:07:11,387 --> 00:07:13,317
Breaking into that club takes years,

152
00:07:13,367 --> 00:07:15,497
and Genesis is learning that the hard way.

153
00:07:15,547 --> 00:07:18,177
Number seven: the BMW iX.

154
00:07:18,227 --> 00:07:21,817
BMW's large electric SUV
used to be a status symbol.

155
00:07:21,867 --> 00:07:25,637
Last month, it found only seven
buyers, down almost 88 per cent.

156
00:07:25,687 --> 00:07:27,837
Part of the reason is BMW itself.

157
00:07:27,887 --> 00:07:32,157
Its new iX3 arrived this year
with a much sharper price,

158
00:07:32,207 --> 00:07:37,897
and in April BMW cut up to $8,900
from the smaller iX1 and iX2.

159
00:07:37,947 --> 00:07:39,277
When a brand's own newer,

160
00:07:39,327 --> 00:07:43,757
cheaper electric SUVs look like better
value, the old flagship gets squeezed.

161
00:07:43,807 --> 00:07:45,577
That's the second big lesson.

162
00:07:45,627 --> 00:07:48,477
Sometimes a car's worst
enemy isn't a rival brand.

163
00:07:48,527 --> 00:07:50,607
It's the next model in its own showroom.

164
00:07:51,321 --> 00:07:54,471
Quick favour before the top six
because this is where it gets really

165
00:07:54,521 --> 00:07:55,491
surprising.

166
00:07:55,541 --> 00:07:57,091
Have you looked at any of these cars?

167
00:07:57,141 --> 00:07:58,211
Or do you own one?

168
00:07:58,261 --> 00:08:00,271
Tell me in the comments I read them all.

169
00:08:00,321 --> 00:08:01,351
And if you want honest,

170
00:08:01,401 --> 00:08:05,051
numbers-first videos about what's
really happening in Aussie car yards,

171
00:08:05,101 --> 00:08:06,091
hit subscribe.

172
00:08:06,141 --> 00:08:08,641
It's free and it genuinely
helps the channel.

173
00:08:10,456 --> 00:08:11,827
Number six: the Polestar 3.

174
00:08:11,877 --> 00:08:16,287
This is a beautifully built, fast
electric SUV with a huge price tag.

175
00:08:16,337 --> 00:08:21,707
The rear-motor version starts at
$116,700 before on-road costs,

176
00:08:21,757 --> 00:08:25,247
and the dual-motor at $131,100.

177
00:08:25,297 --> 00:08:30,187
In September, Polestar sold six of
them in Australia, down 88.5 per cent.

178
00:08:30,237 --> 00:08:33,667
Even Polestar's global boss admits
the brand got its pricing wrong.

179
00:08:33,717 --> 00:08:35,767
In May 2026,

180
00:08:35,817 --> 00:08:39,287
chief executive Michael Lohscheller told
CarsGuide that when Polestar was set

181
00:08:39,337 --> 00:08:43,107
up, it was "maybe a bit too high and
too niche and maybe also a bit too

182
00:08:43,157 --> 00:08:46,667
expensive." He also admitted the
company is still "in a loss-making

183
00:08:46,717 --> 00:08:50,387
situation." That's an extraordinary thing
for the head of a car company to say

184
00:08:50,437 --> 00:08:51,367
out loud.

185
00:08:51,417 --> 00:08:54,167
Number five: the Jeep
Wrangler and Gladiator.

186
00:08:54,217 --> 00:08:56,867
These are icons the original off-roaders.

187
00:08:56,917 --> 00:09:00,647
But last month, the Wrangler sold
nine and the Gladiator ute sold five.

188
00:09:00,697 --> 00:09:04,767
The Wrangler was down 77 per cent
and the Gladiator 80 per cent.

189
00:09:04,817 --> 00:09:08,027
The whole Jeep brand sold
sixteen cars for the month.

190
00:09:08,077 --> 00:09:09,377
Price is a big part of it.

191
00:09:09,427 --> 00:09:13,077
CarSauce reported that the cheapest
four-door Wrangler went from around

192
00:09:13,127 --> 00:09:19,207
$37,000 in 2014 to $75,950
before on-road costs.

193
00:09:19,257 --> 00:09:20,267
At that price,

194
00:09:20,317 --> 00:09:22,567
buyers are comparing it
with a LandCruiser Prado,

195
00:09:22,617 --> 00:09:26,447
a Ford Everest, or a Chinese
4x4 with a lot more equipment.

196
00:09:26,497 --> 00:09:27,887
Jeep says it's committed to Australia.

197
00:09:27,937 --> 00:09:30,917
But right now, the showroom
traffic isn't there.

198
00:09:32,577 --> 00:09:35,471
Number four: the Alfa
Romeo Tonale and Stelvio.

199
00:09:35,521 --> 00:09:39,131
Alfa Romeo has one of the most
passionate fan bases in the car world.

200
00:09:39,181 --> 00:09:41,051
But passion doesn't pay the bills.

201
00:09:41,101 --> 00:09:44,951
In September, the Tonale
small SUV registered two.

202
00:09:45,001 --> 00:09:47,571
The bigger Stelvio also registered two.

203
00:09:47,621 --> 00:09:53,791
The updated Tonale starts at $64,990
before on-road costs for a small

204
00:09:53,841 --> 00:09:55,091
SUV.

205
00:09:55,141 --> 00:09:58,491
Alfa has run deals with more than
ten thousand dollars off in the past,

206
00:09:58,541 --> 00:10:01,561
and the brand as a whole
sold just 21 cars that month.

207
00:10:01,611 --> 00:10:03,411
Think about that for a moment.

208
00:10:03,461 --> 00:10:04,891
Two Tonales in a month,

209
00:10:04,941 --> 00:10:07,071
while a single Chinese small SUV,

210
00:10:07,121 --> 00:10:10,071
the Chery Tiggo 4, sold
more than two thousand.

211
00:10:10,121 --> 00:10:13,071
Brand heritage counts for
a lot less than it used to.

212
00:10:13,121 --> 00:10:15,451
Number three: the Fiat 500.

213
00:10:15,501 --> 00:10:19,451
The cute little Fiat 500 was once
a common sight in every city.

214
00:10:19,501 --> 00:10:21,311
In September 2026,

215
00:10:21,361 --> 00:10:26,471
the Fiat 500 and Abarth line found
two buyers, down almost 95 per cent.

216
00:10:26,521 --> 00:10:30,411
Fiat already tried the price-cut
route with the electric 500e.

217
00:10:30,461 --> 00:10:36,651
In 2025, it dropped the 500e La Prima
from $52,500 before on-road costs

218
00:10:36,701 --> 00:10:39,591
to $38,990 drive-away.

219
00:10:39,641 --> 00:10:44,591
Fiat said the deal was to "stimulate
sales and clear out existing stock." When

220
00:10:44,641 --> 00:10:47,591
a brand says the words "clear
out existing stock" out loud,

221
00:10:47,641 --> 00:10:48,761
you know things are tough.

222
00:10:49,475 --> 00:10:52,085
Number two: the Peugeot 308.

223
00:10:52,135 --> 00:10:53,855
This one is almost hard to believe.

224
00:10:53,905 --> 00:10:56,695
The Peugeot 308 is a stylish,

225
00:10:56,745 --> 00:11:01,885
well-reviewed small car, sold as a
petrol hatch and as an electric e-308.

226
00:11:01,935 --> 00:11:03,785
In September, it found two buyers.

227
00:11:03,835 --> 00:11:07,352
For the whole of 2026 so
far, the tally is seventeen.

228
00:11:07,402 --> 00:11:11,065
Seventeen cars in nine months,
across the entire country.

229
00:11:11,115 --> 00:11:13,665
And the 308's problem goes beyond the car.

230
00:11:13,715 --> 00:11:17,645
In July 2026, Peugeot's
importer, Inchcape,

231
00:11:17,695 --> 00:11:20,685
agreed to end its partnership
with Stellantis in Australia.

232
00:11:20,735 --> 00:11:23,845
Stellantis says Peugeot "has
a strong future in Australia".

233
00:11:23,895 --> 00:11:24,845
But if you're a buyer,

234
00:11:24,895 --> 00:11:28,545
uncertainty like that makes you
nervous and nervous buyers don't sign

235
00:11:28,595 --> 00:11:29,605
contracts.

236
00:11:29,655 --> 00:11:31,905
And number one: the Hyundai Ioniq 9.

237
00:11:31,955 --> 00:11:33,345
The car we started with.

238
00:11:33,395 --> 00:11:34,605
One sale in September.

239
00:11:34,655 --> 00:11:37,725
Sixty-five for the whole of 2026 so far,

240
00:11:37,775 --> 00:11:40,345
and only forty in 2025, its launch year.

241
00:11:40,395 --> 00:11:44,105
This is a seven-seat electric SUV
from one of the biggest brands in the

242
00:11:44,155 --> 00:11:48,205
country a brand that sold more than
five thousand cars last month alone.

243
00:11:48,255 --> 00:11:49,445
So what went wrong?

244
00:11:49,495 --> 00:11:53,825
Price is part of it the top-spec
Calligraphy is listed at around $128,000

245
00:11:53,875 --> 00:11:55,905
drive-away in Sydney.

246
00:11:55,955 --> 00:11:59,685
Competition is part of it too, with
cheaper Chinese seven-seaters arriving.

247
00:11:59,735 --> 00:12:02,285
But Hyundai's own boss
has been brutally honest.

248
00:12:02,335 --> 00:12:05,305
At the Ioniq 9's launch in August 2025,

249
00:12:05,355 --> 00:12:07,745
Hyundai Australia's new
chief executive, Don Romano,

250
00:12:07,795 --> 00:12:12,065
said: "We do a terrible job with our
EVs." He said Hyundai's electric market

251
00:12:12,115 --> 00:12:16,565
share was "extremely low relative to our
market share of total vehicles." More

252
00:12:16,615 --> 00:12:20,315
than a year later, the sales numbers
show how big that job still is.

253
00:12:21,058 --> 00:12:22,128
Before we move on,

254
00:12:22,178 --> 00:12:25,688
a quick-fire round of cars that just
missed the list because the pattern is

255
00:12:25,738 --> 00:12:27,928
everywhere once you start looking.

256
00:12:27,978 --> 00:12:29,868
The Mercedes-Benz C-Class,

257
00:12:29,918 --> 00:12:32,228
once a staple of every leafy suburb:

258
00:12:32,278 --> 00:12:36,048
39 registrations in September,
down almost 58 per cent.

259
00:12:36,098 --> 00:12:40,668
The Volvo XC90 seven-seater: 33, down 62.

260
00:12:40,718 --> 00:12:44,148
The Mazda CX-90: 36, down a third.

261
00:12:44,198 --> 00:12:46,308
The Hyundai Sonata: 16.

262
00:12:46,358 --> 00:12:47,588
The Skoda Superb,

263
00:12:47,638 --> 00:12:50,008
one of the most spacious cars
you can buy for the money:

264
00:12:50,058 --> 00:12:51,928
ten, down more than half.

265
00:12:51,978 --> 00:12:55,088
And the Honda Civic, a nameplate
that used to be everywhere:

266
00:12:55,138 --> 00:12:57,188
55, down 38 per cent.

267
00:12:57,238 --> 00:12:58,348
Notice something?

268
00:12:58,398 --> 00:12:59,768
Most of these are sedans,

269
00:12:59,818 --> 00:13:03,808
big seven-seaters or European models
exactly the kinds of cars being squeezed

270
00:13:03,858 --> 00:13:08,328
hardest by cheaper SUVs, hybrids
and the flood of new Chinese brands.

271
00:13:08,378 --> 00:13:10,428
The Australian market isn't shrinking.

272
00:13:10,478 --> 00:13:11,788
It's being reshuffled,

273
00:13:11,838 --> 00:13:15,228
and some very famous names are on
the wrong side of that reshuffle.

274
00:13:15,278 --> 00:13:19,108
Now, before you assume every big
sales drop means a car is unloved,

275
00:13:19,158 --> 00:13:22,268
here are the cars that look like
disasters in the data but tell a very

276
00:13:22,318 --> 00:13:22,898
different story.

277
00:13:22,948 --> 00:13:25,588
The Toyota LandCruiser 70 Series.

278
00:13:25,638 --> 00:13:28,408
In September, its sales
were down 96 per cent.

279
00:13:28,458 --> 00:13:30,848
Does that mean buyers have
turned their backs on it?

280
00:13:30,898 --> 00:13:31,788
The opposite.

281
00:13:31,838 --> 00:13:35,248
Toyota has repeatedly paused orders
because of strong demand and limited

282
00:13:35,298 --> 00:13:39,488
production, and new Australian
regulations forced a production pause.

283
00:13:39,538 --> 00:13:41,728
Buyers want them; they
just can't get them.

284
00:13:41,778 --> 00:13:43,168
The Toyota Fortuner.

285
00:13:43,218 --> 00:13:44,368
Down 94 per cent.

286
00:13:44,418 --> 00:13:49,008
That's because Toyota confirmed in late
2025 that the Fortuner was being axed

287
00:13:49,058 --> 00:13:51,368
in Australia, with no replacement.

288
00:13:51,418 --> 00:13:53,508
Dealers are simply selling the last cars.

289
00:13:53,558 --> 00:13:55,888
The GWM Ora electric hatch.

290
00:13:55,938 --> 00:13:58,988
One sale last month,
down almost 99 per cent.

291
00:13:59,038 --> 00:14:03,528
It's been dropped, and GWM is
replacing it with the new Ora 5 SUV.

292
00:14:03,578 --> 00:14:05,288
And the Volkswagen T-Roc.

293
00:14:05,338 --> 00:14:09,628
Down 84 per cent but a new-generation
model is due here in 2027,

294
00:14:09,678 --> 00:14:13,768
so buyers are holding off.

295
00:14:13,818 --> 00:14:13,925
The lesson?

296
00:14:13,975 --> 00:14:14,631
A sales collapse can
mean a car is unloved,

297
00:14:14,681 --> 00:14:18,768
or it can mean a car is being replaced
or simply can't be built fast enough.

298
00:14:18,818 --> 00:14:22,258
Before you buy a heavily discounted
car, find out which one it is.

299
00:14:22,970 --> 00:14:24,560
So what does all this mean for you?

300
00:14:24,610 --> 00:14:28,380
If you're buying, cars that aren't
selling are where the biggest deals live.

301
00:14:28,430 --> 00:14:31,440
We've seen Mazda cut up to $8,051,

302
00:14:31,490 --> 00:14:34,180
Genesis offer up to $10,000 off,

303
00:14:34,230 --> 00:14:37,000
BMW trim up to $8,900,

304
00:14:37,050 --> 00:14:40,936
and Fiat drop the electric 500e to
under thirty-nine thousand dollars

305
00:14:40,986 --> 00:14:42,640
drive-away to clear stock.

306
00:14:42,690 --> 00:14:44,920
If one of these cars genuinely suits you,

307
00:14:44,970 --> 00:14:47,000
ask for a drive-away price in writing,

308
00:14:47,050 --> 00:14:48,940
ask how long the car has been in stock,

309
00:14:48,990 --> 00:14:51,480
and ask whether a newer
model is coming soon.

310
00:14:51,530 --> 00:14:54,740
Old stock is often where the
dealer has the most room to move.

311
00:14:54,790 --> 00:14:55,800
And the end of the year,

312
00:14:55,850 --> 00:14:59,660
when dealers chase their annual targets,
can be one of the best times to ask.

313
00:14:59,710 --> 00:15:01,960
It's also worth asking
about demonstrators.

314
00:15:02,010 --> 00:15:03,560
When a model is slow-moving,

315
00:15:03,610 --> 00:15:06,860
dealers often have demo cars with
a few thousand kilometres on them,

316
00:15:06,910 --> 00:15:09,300
still covered by most
of the new-car warranty.

317
00:15:09,350 --> 00:15:13,600
On a car that's already heavily discounted,
a demo can take off another chunk.

318
00:15:13,650 --> 00:15:15,000
Just check the build date,

319
00:15:15,050 --> 00:15:17,180
the warranty start date
and the service history,

320
00:15:17,230 --> 00:15:20,180
and make sure the price
reflects any wear and tear.

321
00:15:20,230 --> 00:15:21,640
And always compare.

322
00:15:21,690 --> 00:15:24,220
If a slow seller is ten
thousand dollars off,

323
00:15:24,270 --> 00:15:27,240
line it up against the best-selling
alternatives in the same class,

324
00:15:27,290 --> 00:15:28,940
with their deals included.

325
00:15:28,990 --> 00:15:31,640
Sometimes the discounted
car is a genuine bargain.

326
00:15:31,690 --> 00:15:33,780
Sometimes the popular car, at full price,

327
00:15:33,830 --> 00:15:36,280
is still better value
once you add in resale.

328
00:15:36,330 --> 00:15:37,300
But be careful.

329
00:15:37,350 --> 00:15:40,740
A car that's hard to sell new is
usually hard to sell used, too.

330
00:15:40,790 --> 00:15:43,540
Expect faster depreciation,
and plan to keep it longer.

331
00:15:43,590 --> 00:15:45,920
Check the warranty, the service plan,

332
00:15:45,970 --> 00:15:49,240
and how far you'll have to travel for
servicing and parts especially for

333
00:15:49,290 --> 00:15:52,440
brands with small dealer
networks or uncertain futures.

334
00:15:52,490 --> 00:15:55,480
And if you already own one
of these cars, don't panic.

335
00:15:55,530 --> 00:15:59,440
Low new-car sales don't change your
warranty or your consumer rights.

336
00:15:59,490 --> 00:16:01,220
Keep your service history up to date,

337
00:16:01,270 --> 00:16:02,600
and if you're thinking of selling,

338
00:16:02,650 --> 00:16:05,140
get a few valuations
before you trade it in.

339
00:16:05,190 --> 00:16:09,080
So, twelve new cars that Australians
just aren't buying right now from the

340
00:16:09,130 --> 00:16:12,680
Volkswagen ID.4 all the
way to the Hyundai Ioniq 9,

341
00:16:12,730 --> 00:16:15,320
with one single sale in an entire month.

342
00:16:15,370 --> 00:16:17,720
If this helped, hit like, subscribe,

343
00:16:17,770 --> 00:16:20,240
and share it with someone
who's about to buy a new car.

344
00:16:20,290 --> 00:16:23,360
Tell me in the comments: which
of these surprised you the most?

345
00:16:23,410 --> 00:16:24,280
And in the next video,

346
00:16:24,330 --> 00:16:27,920
we're looking at the ute price war
because Toyota and Ford have started

347
00:16:27,970 --> 00:16:30,880
slashing prices on Australia's
favourite vehicles.

348
00:16:30,930 --> 00:16:31,750
See you there.
